DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Plan for higher rates, not cuts.</b> October CPI came in hot (0.4%, core 0.3%) and markets now price about a 90% chance of a December hike, possibly a half point; avoid new floating-rate or high-interest debt and keep an emergency cash buffer.",
"<b>Keep investing regularly, not all at once.</b> Fear & Greed is 33 (Fear) and new lows still beat new highs (47 vs 116), so steady dollar-cost averaging into broad funds beats trying to time the bottom.",
"<b>Cash and short bonds pay you to wait.</b> With the 10Y near 5% and the 2Y up 18bp in a day, short-term deposits or bond funds are a fair place for money you need within a year or two.",
"<b>Don't let one AI stock decide your year.</b> Nvidia fell about 9.5% in two days on CEO governance news while CoreWeave jumped after hours; a broad or equal-weight fund spreads that risk.",
"<b>Fuel is getting cheaper, slowly.</b> Brent briefly broke $90 and diesel eased to ~$6.16; good for budgets, but Hormuz attacks mean prices can spike again.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a rocket.</b> It fell ~2.7% to about $4,030 on rate-hike bets; keep it a small slice and don't chase dips with borrowed money.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> BTC slid to ~$73.7k as yields rose; rate hikes are a headwind, so only hold what you can leave alone.",
"<b>Thai investors: the bounce has better support today.</b> The SET jumped 1.58% to 1,496 with foreigners net buyers (+฿682M) after the cabinet approved data-center rules; resistance is 1,500. In our dividend table, SPALI, ICHI, PTTEP, AP, TVO and PTT still trade at or below their buy zones (green) — check payout safety first.",
"<b>Peace headlines aren't a signed deal.</b> Rubio says no major combat is needed, but Iran's demands and the Ukraine ceasefire are unresolved; don't bet big on one headline."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 33 = Fear, up slightly from 32 Monday and 24 a week ago. Price strength, breadth, VIX and junk bonds read neutral, but momentum, put/call and safe-haven demand are still in extreme fear."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~42 = Elevated (down from ~43): Rubio saying major combat against Iran isn't needed and the Abu Dhabi Ukraine talks offset continuing Hormuz shipping attacks."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 13.2 = extreme fear: the index is still below its recent trend and slipped 0.38% Tuesday."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 47.6 = neutral on CNN's measure, but on the NYSE lows still dominate (47 highs vs 116 lows Tuesday)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 50.2 = neutral: no strong tilt either way after Monday's broad rally and Tuesday's dip."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 16.2 = extreme fear: investors keep buying protection as Fed-hike bets grow."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. Reading 50 = neutral: volatility stayed contained even after the hot CPI."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 10.6 = extreme fear: bonds have beaten stocks over the recent window, though less so than last week."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 46.4 = neutral, improving from 42.4 Monday; CoreWeave's solid outlook eased AI-debt worries."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 55 (from 56): Rubio says no major combat is needed as sanctions bite, though Iran's demands are unresolved. Iran isn't a confirmed nuclear state."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 38 (flat): ~4 hours of Abu Dhabi talks, little headway on a ceasefire or Donbas; day two on 11 Nov."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 73 (flat): ship attacks near Hormuz continue, though Gulf oil flows have largely recovered."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 12 (flat): G7 in Paris, Qatar's briefings and the Abu Dhabi trilateral."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 30 (flat): no explicit nuclear threats in our sources; IAEA access remains part of Qatar's plan."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,521 Tuesday (−0.38%) after hot CPI; 4.1% below its record, below its 50-day average."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. −0.30% Tuesday to about 52,232."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. −0.74% Tuesday to about 25,066 as Nvidia fell 5.5%; 9.6% below its record."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.99% Tuesday (+11bp) after hot CPI — right at the 5% line."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$86.0 (−0.9%) Tuesday, lowest close since 31 Aug, on Iran de-escalation hopes."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$91.5 (−1.2%); briefly under $90 for the first time since August."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$6.16/gal (AAA, 10 Nov), easing but still above $6; the 22 Sep record was $6.53."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$4,035 (−2.6%) after hot CPI lifted the dollar and yields; $4,000 is the nearby support."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$73.7k = bearish: higher yields and hike bets weigh; $73k is the line to watch."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00%, held on 28 Oct; next decision 8-9 Dec, where a hike is now about 90% priced."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. October rose 0.4% MoM (est. 0.3%) and core 0.3% (est. 0.2%); no official YoY because of last year's data gap, but the Cleveland Fed estimates ~3.8%, well above the Fed's 2% goal."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. +6.3% in a year, the biggest since 2022; October PPI is due Fri 13 Nov (8:30pm Bangkok)."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). About 90% for a quarter-point hike on 9 Dec after CPI, with some bets on half a point."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. The Bloomberg dollar gauge rose 0.5% Tuesday on hot CPI; the euro fell to $1.1165."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~158.75 = a weak yen (−0.5% Tuesday) as US yields jumped; the BOJ held at 1.25%."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) in October; its raised outlook on 10 Nov eased some AI-debt fears."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct in a unanimous vote (fourth hold in a row); the BoT raised its 2026 growth forecast to 2.4%, sees inflation at 2.1% and is watching oil and El Niño risks."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,496.31 Tue 10 Nov (+1.58%) on DELTA and data-center rules; 1,500 is the next resistance."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. +฿681.78M on 10 Nov (after −฿2.5B on 9 Nov); local institutions +฿1,877M, Thai retail −฿2,243M (SET via HoonSmart)."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};

